#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:170
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computed from six facts read off the records — report status, data hash known, unexecuted cases, the checker's agreement, failed and passed cases — by the table the plan's `exitCriteria` names (resolved dynamically; if unresolvable, routes to undetermined and never silently falls back to default). Supplying the branch by hand is refused."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:138
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every case in dependency order. A case is executed or explicitly `skipped` with its reason; a case that simply has no verdict is a finding, because it cannot be told from a case nobody ran."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:137
#. Diagram label
msgid "Execute every case, or skip it with a reason"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Executing a `test-plan/v1` against a system under test and taking the result to a certification decision: requested by (or for) the system, run by a tester, re-executed in sample by an untainted checker, decided by a certifier through the plan's exit-criteria table, and signed through `qa-report-signing.bpmn`. You are in this process when somebody wants a system — a skill, an agent, a tool, a machine, an IG or a process — certified against a named plan. Executing a plan with no certification in view is still this process; it ends at `undetermined` or `refused` without anything being signed. The run, the report and the certification are three records, and they point backwards: the run at the plan, the report at the run, the certification at the report. The certification is a judgement and lives under the declared `attestations` graph, on main; the report is derived and lives on the `qa-reports` branch."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:169
#. Diagram label
msgid "Exit criteria met?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:221
#. Diagram label
msgid "File the signed certification"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:159
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Given the plan, the bound data and a sample of case ids — not the report. Says `agree`, `disagree` or `unknown`; `unknown` (could not run) is said as plainly as a disagreement, because the table reads both the same way and an unknown read as agreement certifies on one party's word."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:261
#. Diagram label
msgid "How did it end?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:108
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Name the plan by id AND version, and the system under test by actor id. The actor must carry the `systemUnderTest` facet: an actor that has not said it can be tested is not run against a plan by default. The bean this instance tracks is claimed here."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:281
#. Diagram label
msgid "not yours"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:253
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:241
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:128
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Per bean `vm6m`: a fixed set is a committed path and counts as evidence only once reviewed; a generated set is template + params + seed and is never materialised. Both feed the run's data hash, and nothing that feeds the process hash may feed it too."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:258
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:242
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:158
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-execute a sample, blind to the tester's verdicts"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:248
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

