msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:272
#. Diagram label
msgid "refused"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:107
#. Diagram label
msgid "Request certification of the system against plan P"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:65
#. Diagram label
msgid "Requester / system under test"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:117
#. Diagram label
msgid "Resolve the plan"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the plan against the system: resolves it, binds its fixed or generated test data, executes every case or skips it with a reason, and writes the `folio-test-run/v1` and the `test-report/v1`. Untainted from the system under test — never the same actor — and it does not certify: what it writes is what the certifier decides on."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:211
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sign the certification"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:94
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Signs the certification and files it. Reached only from `certified`: a refusal and an undetermined result are recorded by the certifier and signed by nobody. The signature itself is `qa-report-signing.bpmn`, called unchanged, whose own gateway chooses the API or a human release authority by the signer's reach."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:254
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Test-plan execution"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Test-plan execution — request, run, check, certify, sign"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Tester"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The accountable party for the decision, a specialisation of the stakeholder. The gateway is computed from the plan's exit-criteria table; what the certifier adds, and what makes it a judgement, is recording the decision under their name. Never the tester and never the system under test."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:181
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The judgement: the certifier records, under their own name, that the system meets plan P at this version on this run. It is written under the declared `attestations` graph beside the other judgements, never on the `qa-reports` branch with derived results. A user task, so no agent or pipeline can fill it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:118
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan parses, names at least one `req:` requirement, its `exitCriteria` resolves to a decision in a `.dmn` that exists, and its `scope.kind` is the system's facet kind. A plan that does not resolve is not run — `test-plan-resolves` audits the same join afterwards. Reads a `test-plan/v1`."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:149
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The run records `plan {id, version}` and `sut {actor, version, reach}` with its data and process hashes; the report rolls up per plan, never across plans, and goes to the `qa-reports` branch at `tests/plan/sut/run/`. No verdict in it may name the system under test as its reviewer. Writes a `folio-test-run/v1` and a `test-report/v1`."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:222
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signed certification goes under the declared `attestations` graph on main (owner ruling D2 (a), D5 default), pointing at the report it certifies. The bean resolves here, once the process has actually finished. Files it as `qa-attestations/v1`."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The system under test, or whoever speaks for it, asking for certification against plan P at a named version. Its only task is the request, and that is the design rather than an omission: the system under test never writes a verdict about itself, so after this lane it is the SUBJECT of the process and never a performer in it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:202
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The third state: which fact kept the table from deciding — a run not finished, an unknown data hash, an unexecuted case, a checker that disagreed or could not run, or nothing passed. A note and not a resolution, because the request is still open: it needs a re-run or an adjudication, not a verdict."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:273
#. Diagram label
msgid "undetermined"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:237
#. Diagram label
msgid "Undetermined — nothing signed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Untainted checker"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:262
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which outcome the bean was closed with, so each ends at its own named end event. The bean is closed once, on every path (bpmn-authoring: open and close the bean at the top, once)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn:148
#. Diagram label
msgid "Write the test run and the test report"
msgstr ""
